            "value": false
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "use": "tell",
      "phase": "end of round",
      "label": "public state",
      "to": "all",
      "text": "End of round {round}. Dice: Red {die_red}, Blue {die_blue}, Green {die_green}, Yellow {die_yellow}, Purple {die_purple}. Gold: seat 1 {players[0].gold}, seat 2 {players[1].gold}, seat 3 {players[2].gold}. Public records: seat 1 [{players[0].public_record}], seat 2 [{players[1].public_record}], seat 3 [{players[2].public_record}]."
    },
    {
      "use": "update",
      "phase": "end of round",
      "label": "score the colours",
      "when": {
        "calc": "round >= rounds"
      },
      "do": [
        {
          "adjust": {
            "players": "all",
            "key": "vp",
            "value": {
              "calc": "(die_red if you.red > max([p.red for p in players if p.seat != you.seat]) else 0) + (die_blue if you.blue > max([p.blue for p in players if p.seat != you.seat]) else 0) + (die_green if you.green > max([p.green for p in players if p.seat != you.seat]) else 0) + (die_yellow if you.yellow > max([p.yellow for p in players if p.seat != you.seat]) else 0) + (die_purple if you.purple > max([p.purple for p in players if p.seat != you.seat]) else 0)"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "use": "check",
      "phase": "end of round",
      "label": "after round 12",
      "when": {
        "calc": "round >= rounds"
      },
      "against": [
        "over"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "end": {
    "over": {
      "when": {
        "calc": "round >= rounds"
      },
      "rank_by": "you.vp * 1000 + you.gold",
      "text": "Winner: {result}. Final VP (gold): seat 1 {players[0].vp} ({players[0].gold}), seat 2 {players[1].vp} ({players[1].gold}), seat 3 {players[2].vp} ({players[2].gold}); dice Red {die_red}, Blue {die_blue}, Green {die_green}, Yellow {die_yellow}, Purple {die_purple}."
    }
  },
  "limits": {
    "rounds": 12,
    "rounds_max": 13,
    "actions_max": 1000,
    "deadline_s": 120
  },
  "rules": "Three players, seats 1, 2 and 3. The deck has {deck_size} cards and its makeup is public: {colour_cards_total} colour cards in five colours (Red, Blue, Green, Yellow, Purple), each colour with values 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 4; {gold_cards} Gold cards worth {gold_card_small}, {gold_card_mid} and {gold_card_large} gold; and {church_cards} Church cards. The deck is shuffled once. Each player starts with {starting_gold} gold, 0 in every colour, an empty public record and a church flag set to No. Five colour dice each start at {die_start}; a die can never go below {die_min} or above {die_max}.\n\nThe game lasts exactly {rounds} rounds. The active player in rounds 1 to 12 is, in order: seat 1, 2, 3, 2, 3, 1, 3, 1, 2, 1, 2, 3. The active player's next seat is cyclic: 1 to 2, 2 to 3, 3 to 1.\n\nCARD EFFECTS (whenever a player receives a card): a colour card adds its value to that player's total in its colour. A Gold card adds its gold to that player's purse. A Church card sets that player's church flag to Yes; if the flag is already Yes, the card has no further effect this round. A player gets at most one church action per round, no matter how many Church cards they acquire.\n\nEACH ROUND:\n1. The round number and active player are announced.\n2. The top {cards_per_round} cards of the deck are dealt and shown only to the active player.\n3. SPLIT: the active player assigns the three cards, one each, to KEEP, AUCTION and GIVE, choosing one of the {split_options} possible assignments.\n4. The KEEP card goes to the active player face-down and takes effect. Only that player knows what it was. Purses are public, so a gold gain reveals a kept Gold card.\n5. The GIVE card is revealed, goes to the active player's next seat, takes effect, and is added to that player's public record.\n6. The AUCTION card is revealed to everyone.\n7. TALK: all three players write one short message at the same time; all messages are shown together. Talk is not binding.\n8. BID: all three players secretly and at the same time bid a whole number from {min_bid} up to their current gold.\n9. All bids are revealed. If exactly one player made the highest bid and it is above {winning_bid_must_exceed}, that player pays that much gold, which leaves the game, and takes the auction card, which takes effect and is added to their public record. Otherwise (a tie for the top bid, or all bids 0) the card is discarded and nobody pays.\n10. CHURCH: every player whose church flag is Yes chooses, all at the same time, exactly one of {church_options} options: raise Red, lower Red, raise Blue, lower Blue, raise Green, lower Green, raise Yellow, lower Yellow, raise Purple, lower Purple, each by {die_step}. Choices are applied in seat order 1, 2, 3, each clamped to the range {die_min}-{die_max} (raising a 6 or lowering a 1 does nothing). If no flag is Yes, this step is skipped.\n11. All church flags are reset to No.\n12. Public state is announced: the five die values, each player's gold and each player's public record. Kept cards and true colour totals are not shown.\n\nEND OF GAME (after round {rounds}; all {deck_size} cards have been dealt): for each colour, compare the three players' true totals in that colour, kept cards included. If one player alone has the highest total, that player scores VP equal to that colour's final die value. If the highest total is tied, nobody scores that colour. Each player's VP is the sum of the colours they won. The player with the most VP wins. If VP is tied at the top, the tied player with the most remaining gold wins. If that is also tied, the game is a draw among those players, who share the win."
}
